WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.395
FedRAMP uses impact levels to help categorize cloud systems based on the

00:00:04.395 --> 00:00:06.542
potential impact of a security incident.

00:00:06.542 --> 00:00:09.405
Common impact levels include Low, Moderate, and High.

00:00:09.405 --> 00:00:12.984
Impact levels help determine appropriate security requirements based on risk.

00:00:12.984 --> 00:00:18.710
A system that could create higher impact if compromised generally requires a stronger set of safeguards,

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:20.141
controls, documentation, and monitoring.

00:00:20.141 --> 00:00:24.436
Low impact systems may involve information or functions where a security event

00:00:24.436 --> 00:00:26.225
would have limited adverse effect.

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:30.162
Moderate and High impact systems involve progressively greater concern for confidentiality,

00:00:30.162 --> 00:00:31.235
integrity, or availability.

00:00:31.235 --> 00:00:35.888
These categories help agencies and cloud providers align security effort with system sensitivity.

00:00:35.888 --> 00:00:41.256
The goal is not to apply the same level of rigor to every cloud service,

00:00:41.256 --> 00:00:44.477
but to match expectations to risk and mission context.

00:00:44.477 --> 00:00:47.698
Impact level affects control baselines, assessment expectations, monitoring activities,

00:00:47.698 --> 00:00:50.561
and the evidence that stakeholders need to review.

00:00:50.561 --> 00:00:54.855
It also helps frame conversations about whether a service is appropriate for

00:00:54.855 --> 00:00:56.645
a specific agency use case.

00:00:56.645 --> 00:01:00.939
Understanding impact levels is useful for engineers and managers because design decisions

00:01:00.939 --> 00:01:04.876
can affect how a cloud service supports the expected security posture.

00:01:04.876 --> 00:01:08.455
The practical message is that FedRAMP authorization is risk based.

00:01:08.455 --> 00:01:11.318
Higher impact does not simply mean more paperwork;

00:01:11.318 --> 00:01:16.686
it means a stronger need to show that security controls are implemented and maintained appropriately.

00:01:16.686 --> 00:01:18.475
Impact levels also influence planning.

00:01:18.475 --> 00:01:22.054
Teams need to understand the intended customer, data, mission use,

00:01:22.054 --> 00:01:27.780
and operating environment early enough to design controls and evidence processes that fit the expected level.
